# Day 02 - AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)

## Topics Covered
- What is IAM?
- IAM Users
- IAM Groups
- IAM Roles
- IAM Policies
- Root User vs IAM User
- Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)

## Hands-on
- Created an IAM User
- Assigned Permissions
- Explored Managed Policies

## Key Learnings
- IAM provides secure access to AWS resources.
- Follow the Principle of Least Privilege.
- Avoid using the Root User for daily tasks.

